From 4efbed3ed0c93efc9ef9cae9ae871e8edb8a79f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:20:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sidebar): amber 'attention' stripe for done kanban cards
 a plugin check flags [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A session whose kanban cards were all done painted green even when a card's
handoff admitted part of the work was dropped ('split to follow-up') and no
follow-up card existed. kanban_session_activity gains register_done_check(name,
fn): plugins judge each card completed in the last 24 h, and session rows with
a flagged card get kanban_attention. The renderer turns the would-be green
'done' stripe into amber 'attention' (a warning count on the row, a ⌘]/⌘[
stop, keeps automated rows visible). Nothing registered = no field, no reads.
